title: Overlord RAT Execution as MsgEdgeUpdate from User AppData
id: 9fe472a6-ff8f-4d17-abb6-d5dc774c7188
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of the Overlord RAT implant that Cisco Talos attributes to UAT-12643, which copies itself to %APPDATA%\MsgEdgeUpdate.exe and is relaunched through the Zoipers and MsgEdgeUpdate Run values. The same campaign persists through the Windows recovery environment by patching %TARGETOSDRIVE%\Recovery\OEM\ResetConfig.xml, so pair an alert here with a check of that file and with JSON-RPC traffic to Solana endpoints used for the dead-drop resolver.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com/solana-blockchain-transactions/
  - https://malware.news/t/uat-12643-suspected-north-korea-aligned-actor-blends-blockchain-resilience-with-targeted-infostealing/127417
  - https://alcybr.com/blog/talos-finds-uat-12643-hiding-c2-addresses-in-solana-transactions
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/19
tags:
  - attack.t1102
  - attack.t1071
  - attack.t1547
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection_img:
    Image|endswith: '\MsgEdgeUpdate.exe'
  selection_path:
    Image|contains: '\AppData\'
  condition: selection_img and selection_path
falsepositives:
  - Endpoint management or backup agents that legitimately run binaries from per-user AppData; confirm the file name and the Zoipers or MsgEdgeUpdate Run value before isolating
  - Malware sandboxes and threat-intel tooling that detonate Overlord samples under analysis paths
level: high
